        "step_title": "SynoKernel WiFi",
        "items": [
            {
                "desc": "<b>Experimental, at your own risk.</b> These kernel modules are outside of what Synology supports: a module that does not suit the kernel can crash the NAS, and DSM updates may break them. Support is limited: read the documentation, and check the issues already open, before opening one. Do not use them on a NAS you cannot afford to restart or recover."
            },
            {
                "desc": "The kernel modules of this package are <b>not loaded</b> on installation, nor at boot, and DSM does not show their WiFi interfaces in its network settings. Load the driver of your adapter, as root, with the <b>synocli-kernelmodule</b> helper of SynoCli Kernel Tools, then connect with <b>wifi-connect</b> of SynoCli WiFi Tools and the profile of the network:<br><br><code>synocli-kernelmodule list</code><br><code>sudo -i synocli-kernelmodule --profile rtl88x2bu start</code><br><code>sudo -i wifi-connect --profile MyNetwork start</code><br><br>See the <a target=\"_blank\" href=\"https://docs.synocommunity.com/packages/synokernel-wifi/\">package documentation</a> for the adapters it supports, and <a target=\"_blank\" href=\"https://docs.synocommunity.com/packages/synocli-kernel/#loading-modules-at-boot\">Loading modules at boot</a> for the scheduled task that loads them at every startup."
            }
        ]
    }
